<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Maxtel 16-month profit slumps after delays.</title>
<headline>Maxtel 16-month profit slumps after delays.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sixteen months ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     1.7	   vs 5.1</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   0.01	  vs 0.50</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   0.14	  vs 0.43</p>
<p>    Tax			 nil	   vs 0.02</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.23	  vs 0.03</p>
<p>    Turnover		  3.37	  vs 10.62</p>
<p>Full name: Maxtel Ltd</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     0.13 loss   vs 0.08 gain</p>
<p>NOTE - Telecommunications equipment supplier Maxtel said the period had seen difficult trading. This had been due to a delay by one of its principals in launching the new Hagenuk GSM phone and the delay by MTN in implementing its Taxiphone project.</p>
<p>The group aded that there had been several sizeable deals negotiated in the period, but where delivery had only been effective after the financial year-end.</p>
<p>&quot;These will have a significant positive effect on the next reporting period,&quot; the firm said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
